nt.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes 3 attempts in total and waits longer before each retry. I checked it against a local HTTP server and it behaves as intended.\n\n**How it works:**\n- The waits double each time. By default it waits 0.5s before the second attempt and 1s before the third. You can change the starting wait with the new `backoff` argument to `__init__` (default `0.5`).\n- Only a 503 is retried. Any other HTTP error is raised straight away.\n- If all 3 attempts get a 503, the last 503 error is raised to the caller.\n- Network errors and timeouts are not retried. You only asked for 503, so I left those alone.\n- Each failed 503 response is closed before the next attempt, so connections aren't left open.\n\n**Test results** (wait shortened to 0.01s):\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 right away | JSON returned | 1 |\n| 503 twice, then 200 | JSON returned | 3 |\n| 503 three times | 503 error raised | 3 |\n| 500 | 500 error raised | 1 |\n\nThe tests ran as a one-off script and weren't saved, because the repo has no test suite.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 69729, "requests_cache_write": 143741, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7685068, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1790, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial20", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 98, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:50:34.517855+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 23.076, "t_checker_s": 2.429, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s